t(17, 60, """(he has no posterity; his remembrance will be cut off). His disbelief was built on contempt for, and denial of, the idea that Allah would choose a man he saw as weak or without male children.

* Abu Lahab (Abd al-Uzza ibn Abd al-Muttalib): Despite his kinship and his knowledge of the Prophet's ﷺ trustworthiness before the mission, his mental derangement, bigotry and rashness made him deny the matter from its foundations; he was driven by loathing for the convictions of the new religion entirely, and saw it as a pure lie destroying the inheritance of the fathers.

2. Chieftains who disbelieved with the disbelief of "rejection and obstinacy" (while certain of the truthfulness of our Prophet Muhammad ﷺ), and these were the most dangerous group, because they testified to his truthfulness in private and denied it openly:

* Abu Jahl (Amr ibn Hisham): who said plainly (as we have seen) "By Allah, Muhammad is truthful," but the tribal rivalry between Banu Makhzum and Banu Hashim held him back.

* Al-Walid ibn al-Mughirah: who acknowledged the eloquence and inimitability of the Qur'an in private with Abu Bakr, or when he heard it, then turned openly to say "magic handed down," to preserve his political standing among Quraysh.

* Utbah ibn Rabi'ah: who went to negotiate with the Prophet ﷺ, and when he listened to Surat Fussilat he returned to Quraysh with a face other than the one he left with, and said: "By Allah, I have heard words the like of which I have never heard; by Allah, it is neither poetry nor magic," yet he refused to follow out of arrogance and fear of Quraysh's blame.

## Why did some chieftains fall into "real denial"? That is, did they actually think the noble Prophet ﷺ was a liar?
The scholars (such as Ibn al-Qayyim) explain the fall of some great leaders into actual denial by "contemptuous arrogance": they looked at the Prophet ﷺ from a purely class-based, capitalist perspective. As the Qur'an recorded, they said: "Why was this Qur'an not sent down upon a great man from the two towns?" (Az-Zukhruf: 31). Their material contempt for the person of the Prophet ﷺ made their minds close completely to contemplating his miracles, so they thought in their hearts that he was a liar merely because he was not the richest man in Mecca or Ta'if.
In summary: the chieftains were not one copy, O blocked follower; among them was the obstinate one certain of our Prophet's truthfulness, like Abu Jahl, and among them the ignorant denier who truly believed the Prophet was a liar, like Umayyah ibn Khalaf.""")

h(17, 1700, """The disbelief of Quraysh was of two kinds: disbelief of rejection and disbelief of denial""")

t(17, 2350, """Had the polytheists of Quraysh who died in disbelief supposed that Islam is a true and truthful religion, even by 1%, perhaps their fates would have been different (the case here is purely hypothetical, and the idea is a supposition unrelated to written destiny, only to bring the meaning of the post closer), for 1% in a person's mind and thought may be greater than 99%, because it may be the most correct, while the 99% may be the complete error!""")

t(18, 55, """History proves this, just as people's daily life experiences prove it! A 1% supposition that proves true is greater than a 99% supposition that does not!

The result is a manifest loss, or triumph and success!

🟢 The non-deceptive 1% that yields triumph only comes about by purifying the soul of its diseases and filth; then the heart sees, not the eye!
🔴 The deceptive 99% that yields loss comes about by not purifying the soul of its diseases and filth; then the heart does not see, the eye is confused, and you think the misguidance you saw is the manifest truth!""")

h(18, 800, """If people knew how much is in the 1%, many things would change!""")

t(18, 1590, """The polytheists of Quraysh belied the Prophet ﷺ and denied that the Qur'an is revelation from Allah the Exalted .. And some of those who became Muslim on the day of the Conquest denied the Muslims' victory at Hunayn, and one of them cried out: Today the magic is undone .. when they saw the scale tip at the start of Hunayn in favor of Hawazin and Thaqif!

Whoever reviews his conduct by the proof of the Book and the Sunnah and does not believe he is wrong, this does not mean he is right! Your believing that you are right and convincing yourself that you are right is never proof that you are right! Abu Jahl, al-Walid and Abu Lahab believed they were right, and they believed the Prophet ﷺ was neither a prophet nor a messenger .. They believed it very much .. and were very sure .. and very, very confident!

Every day, in every age and every land, people deny a truth recited to their ears and a wisdom spread among them, and kick it with their feet; they confront a right with denial in moments when they are defeated by their whims and their selves, yet they deny and refuse anything but arrogance .. So did a truth die, or a right vanish, or a wisdom perish because the deniers denied?

When denial grows intense in the deniers out of envy and jealousy, or dislike of the light, they think the truth falsehood and see falsehood as truth, merely because they do not believe or are too proud to admit what is right! Is this a method? Is this a mind to rely on to see a truth and perceive a reality and what is right?!""")

h(19, 350, """Not believing something does not mean it is not truth and reality""")

t(19, 930, """This group in society, if any opportunity for moral corruption is announced, will practice dissolution at the highest degrees of their immersion, and in the greatest degrees of complete conviction in what they do! These men and women thirsty for moral dissolution: their problem is not merely the abundance of the source of dissolution; rather, from within they deeply and strongly desire to live moral dissolution, and this is perhaps something old and rooted in the soul of each of them; they longed for it intensely and awaited the moment it would come true!""")

h(19, 1600, """One eager for corruption is a round-the-clock project of dissolution""")

t(19, 2270, """One of the noble brothers may have been confused about what I meant in a post I published this morning about preaching

Mandatory preaching may not be stopped even for a single moment .. But guidance does not have preaching as its highest and greatest cause, and the correction of collective behavior as a whole is never achieved by preaching""")

h(20, 400, """Preaching is Allah's command to every nation with a heavenly message""")

t(20, 1030, """With us in the channel is a sinful narcissist who does not stop for a single day from spewing his intellectual and disbelieving pus in the comments, and from insults and abuse, practicing a daily satanic narcissism .. From the severity of his pain, today the greatest illusion has seized him .. Today he deluded himself that he is able to harm .. And truly I was waiting for this moment .. because you do not know what it means to reach the stage of imagining you are able to harm .. Today the countdown to your end has begun, by the power of Allah the Exalted .. 10 - 9 - 8 - 7 - 6 - 5 - 4 - 3 - 2 ---> ... And finally, after you exhausted us for a long time with daily insults and abuse!""")

h(20, 1750, """In proportion to his pain, the misguided one becomes deluded!""")

t(20, 2395, """If we know, then let us hold to it .. Part of knowledge is fleeing from situations one knows lead to anger .. fleeing from a conversation one knows will drag him into anger .. and fleeing from contact one knows will reopen wounds, so anger results""")

h(21, 450, """The doors of anger open a road to slips of the tongue!""")

t(21, 1105, """One of the righteous kings disguised himself one day to discover the secret of a house before which men stood in a queue. When he entered it he discovered it was a house of ill repute, and when they approached him he avoided touching them. So there is a princely soul and a soul that commands evil, and a person chooses either a crown or a degradation! How beautiful the princely soul is when it is not swept along by what sweeps people along, of wronging oneself or wronging others. Corruption has existed since the earliest times of mankind and is not the offspring of any particular era.

Your rejection of wrong crowns your soul, and your being drawn into wrong degrades your soul .. princely or evil-commanding!""")

h(21, 1850, """The souls of princes and princesses: every soul not drawn by what draws the generality of people!""")

t(21, 2490, """That their role in making their children, as a hoped-for result = zero""")

t(22, 60, """🟢 And that the Maker is Allah alone
🟢 And that the Guide is Allah alone
🟢 And that the Reformer is Allah alone
🟢 And that the One who changes for the better is Allah alone
🟢 And that the One who changes the state is Allah alone
🟢 And that the One who achieves the miracle of change is Allah alone

And that they acknowledge and confess, submitting and surrendering with complete surrender and compliance, that:

🔴 What is called upbringing, and the effort of upbringing = zero before the result
🔴 And that the result never comes about through upbringing
🔴 And that the effect of upbringing on the hoped-for result = zero
🔴 And that 100% of the hoped-for result happens only and exclusively from Allah the Exalted alone.""")

h(22, 950, """Children are not set right until fathers and mothers surrender with a complete, full, undiminished surrender""")

t(22, 1740, """Dictionary definitions and books on upbringing do not concern me, but this is the summary and essence of my understanding, at the age of 50, of the meaning and reality of making a human being. The upbringing that righteous fathers and mothers carry out never, ultimately, absolutely and decisively means making:
🟢 Righteousness
🟢 Piety
🟢 Conscience
🟢 Good character

Rather, it is a commendable effort that "only righteous" fathers and mothers make when they present to their children a model the children follow. But among the prophets were some who raised children, and after raising them the fruit had nothing to do with their effort or toil; and the righteous walked, and still walk, the same path.

So for upbringing I find no definition but the following:
It is the display of the model of moral conduct by the parents in true reality, and the display of a verbal and practical image committed to the Book and the Sunnah, not to customs and traditions, issuing from the parents, seen, heard and witnessed. This is upbringing from A to Z. As for the illusion that upbringing means the fruit, it is an illusion whose consequences are extremely harmful, because it leads to the following in the minds and souls of righteous fathers and mothers:
🔴 That they failed to make a righteous individual
🔴 That Allah is angry with them, since He made their effort scattered dust!

All of these are illusions built on not defining the term!""")

t(23, 100, """So how are our children brought up and how do they become righteous?
You will not understand the answer if you did not understand what was explained before .. and if you grasped what was explained before, here is the answer.

Our children become righteous, are affected by righteous upbringing, come to have a conscience to some degree, and become righteous citizens in word and deed in their societies in only two cases, with no third, even if their fathers and mothers are not righteous:
🟢 The first case: divine guidance by selection, because they have a role in reforming the earth. This kind of making, smelting and hammering is never the case of all children in society .. the model of our master Muhammad, our master Ibrahim, our master Yusuf, our master Musa and our master Isa, peace and blessings be upon them, and the rest of the prophets; and the chosen women Khadijah, Maryam and Asiyah, peace be upon them; and the righteous after them.
🟢 The second case: when society is barred from all sources of corruption, pushed by force toward goodness and the cleanliness of the tongue, the chest, the heart, the mind and the method; then children enter the scope of a coercive, binding social system in which all sources of corrupting the soul are closed.

Apart from that, it is all theoretical theorizing that neither advances nor delays, over which the voices of scholars have grown hoarse for 100 years, and the result is zero.""")

h(23, 1000, """Defining the term: What is upbringing?""")

t(23, 1890, """If we do not understand, we will reach no result

Upbringing affects only behavior, and even this is probable, not certain .. "the tongue and the manner of dealing," and not to a complete degree as many people think. I say this so that fathers and mothers stop the great illusion about their "supposed" great role in making their children!

Even the verbal behavior that sound upbringing affects in children is not affected as most fathers and mothers imagine; children receiving excellent upbringing does not mean their tongues will be disciplined .. this is an illusion

Apart from verbal behavior, in forming the thought, personality and conscience of children, the effect of fathers' and mothers' upbringing on making the conscience = complete zero""")

h(24, 400, """For four years I have been writing: the righteousness of children has nothing to do with upbringing""")

t(24, 990, """The challenge is a drop, and a person thinks it a mountain, while the drop is surrounded by a vast ocean of protection, care and kindness.""")

h(24, 1500, """Great divine kindness means a drop of challenge in the middle of an ocean of protection""")

t(24, 2160, """Defining terms, that is, defining them precisely and wisely and fixing their intellectual and scholarly dimensions without confusion, vagueness, ambiguity or obscurity, leads to verifying the soundness of the ruling reached by ijtihad and its falling on the correct specific person without being tainted by injustice.

In verifying terms, ijtihad on rulings with no explicit text falls into confusion if the mujtahid fails to understand the clear, evident meaning of the ruling or of the one it is passed on.

An example is confusing the term "nashiz" (rebellious wife) with the term "the woman demanding her lawful right"; and of failing to define terms is also "the woman with rights guaranteed by the Sharia" and "the masculinized woman" who does not have the traits of women in word, deed and conduct; and both have rulings!""")

t(25, 60, """... the masculinized woman?! Are all women, in the rulings of the Sharia, women in the first place?! Are all those in the homes women?! Do the rulings of Islam revealed for women apply to them?
My explanation and opinion end here.
------------------------------

The following words are quoted, for the sake of honesty, from an electronic Islamic scholarly source

The masculinized woman!
Defining the term: She is the woman who deliberately, by her full choice and will, without a compelling medical or genetic excuse, abandons her feminine identity and adopts the traits of men in:
Speech: affected roughness of voice and a provocative masculine manner of address.
Deeds and conduct: gait, clothing specific to men, cutting hair in men's distinctive cuts, and trying to impose masculine authority in the social or family sphere

The deterrent and restrictive rulings concerning her:
The legal ruling (strict prohibition): this conduct of hers is forbidden as a major sin, because of the saying of the Prophet ﷺ: "The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the women who imitate men." The curse here is a clear sign of departing from the fitrah.
Loss of some marital rights: if the wife adopts this conduct in word and deed, defies her husband and rebels against her role as a wife, her act is classified in fiqh and in court as "aggravated nushuz." This results in the loss of her maintenance and of her right to claim her share (of nights), and the husband has the right to seek annulment without compensating her if she persists in this conduct, because when he married her he wanted to marry a woman, but the conduct of a woman did not come to him with her.
Discretionary punishment (in court): the mujtahid (the judge) has the right to impose deterrent discretionary punishments (such as rebuke, a fine or temporary imprisonment) aimed at deterrence and reform, to prevent the phenomenon of masculinization from corrupting the family.""")

h(25, 1500, """The rulings of Islam cannot be correctly understood without defining the terms""")

t(25, 2180, """Everything outside al-Bukhari specifically may be right or wrong .. and everything in al-Bukhari is presented to the Book; if it does not agree with the Book, it is an error in its chain even if it is in al-Bukhari. The people of hadith among the Salaf devoted books to this and treated it in detail. As for the Muslims, they are all commanded to learn and understand, each according to his ability and as is easy for him, to clear their accountability before coming before the Lord of the servants. Whoever has not studied should not answer what puzzles people; he must refer matters exclusively to the people of knowledge, for our religion and its rulings are not common property like the market of Ukaz, where every passer-by stops. You have seen how the internet has become full of those who want to bring down the noble hadith root and branch, but this will not happen, by the permission of Allah the Exalted.""")

h(26, 400, """The authentic Sunnah is a light on earth""")

t(26, 1110, """Between the halal and the haram are doubtful matters that only those firmly grounded in knowledge understand and decide. As for the common people giving fatwas on their own about every doubtful matter, that it is halal or haram, this does not end well.""")

h(26, 1700, """The halal of Islam: everything that does not contradict the Book and the Sunnah""")

t(26, 2310, """Will in a human being is created; it is with us as we are born .. it is not acquired .. it is innate in our original creation .. Yes, it grows, develops, flares up and dies down, this is true .. it is affected by rising and falling, but it is one of the foundations of the fitrah .. born in the soul with the birth of the body .. Thoughts are the cause of its flaring up or dying down, and its being affected by thoughts, positively and negatively, sets its path, for will has a path, a way and a method, and its path either lights up or goes dark. When its path lights up and shines, it becomes your army; and when the lamps of its path go out, it (the will) becomes within you an ifrit that sucks out your spirit inside your body. Then not only does your will die down; you collapse and dissolve like a body dissolved in acid.""")

t(27, 100, """So, for your will to become your army, do the following:
1- Need no one but Allah the Exalted
2- Make your real connection with Allah the Exalted
3- Do good with love and sincerity
4- Understand the reality of this world .. the correct reality, not the imagined one people philosophize about
5- Forgive much and punish little, or not punishing is better, higher in rank and greater in loftiness
6- Be indifferent to what is in the hands of all people
7- Take great care of your body and your health
8- Love people sincerely
9- Understand the realities of success and failure in their true meanings
10- Do not be too proud to admit there is something you did not know and were ignorant of
11- Do for people what you would like them to do for you
12- Never walk behind the crowds
13- Free your mind from inherited customs that all contradict the religion
14- Understand the reality of your death correctly""")

h(27, 1000, """Will is the prisoner of your thoughts. Correct them so you may live honorably!""")

t(27, 1845, """Paradise and Hell are proof of the existence of the mind .. the existence of the mind is proof of the existence of choice .. the existence of choice is proof of the existence of will .. the existence of will is proof that the claim of being forced into evil, falsehood and injustice falls .. the fall of the claim of being forced into evil, falsehood and injustice is proof of a human's ability to realize the will to do good on earth .. and the certain establishment of a human's ability to do good on earth is proof that any human can pass his day in peace and safety, whether mixing with people or secluded!

Therefore, the bad day is 90% your will, and the claim that others deprive you of your inner calm is an incorrect claim, whose cause is either:
🔴 Ignorance that you possess a real will to protect yourself, and ignorance of its existence in you
🔴 Or your desire for conflict and your love of it, because it achieves sick psychological goals for you
🔴 Or your fear of protecting yourself from others wrecking your mood, because they make you weak and you have grown used to fearing them
🔴 Or ignorance of your self's right, by Sharia and religion, to live a good life
🔴 Or ignorance that the religion does not give any creature, whoever he is, the right to wreck your mood
🔴 Or your inability to devise solutions to keep yourself away from the people of harm, because of your helplessness
🔴 Or a weakness of personality that prevents you from frightening the people of harm to keep their harm away from you; for the people of harm are madmen, without exaggeration, and there is no way to stop their harm except by frightening them""")

h(28, 400, """Man is the prisoner of his mind. What you tell your mind, your self carries out!""")

t(28, 1175, """A general sentence and a general thought that it is important to reach every person .. I do not mean anyone specific by it .. nor do I mean to point to a particular person""")

h(28, 1700, """The greatest degree of strength: to be at peace in a tent with a date and water, as if you were in a palace!""")

t(28, 2340, """Walking according to people's patterns leaves you stuck with them. Destiny, if it is decreed for you to be poor for 10 years, for example, is decreed; but there is a door that will always remain open to you despite the compulsion of destiny, and that is the door of your effort and using your mind .. I remember a year of not finding work, then work for years, then another year of not getting work .. then work for years .. then a third year of not getting work .. then work for years

In the first year of unemployment, the year was very hard because it was the first experience .. When its pains had passed,""")

t(29, 60, """I realized that the job market is treacherous, so with the help of Allah the Exalted I made my own individual work for myself .. a profession alongside the profession, to play the role of the backup. Then came the second year of unemployment, and it was a year with zero financial problems, because the backup profession worked well .. Then work came again .. and the backup profession was neglected .. Then came the third year of unemployment, and the context moved from the relationship with the backup profession to the relationship with Allah the Exalted, and the astonishing happened .. unemployment and no harm .. Then came years when the backup profession worked again .. Then an international decision was issued to wreck the backup profession (authorship and writing), so the year of unemployment returned anew, the distortions of job markets in the world grew more and more, and the difficulties of finding real work increased .. The job market globally drowned in hiring not based on putting a person in the right place. But the relationship with Allah the Exalted was above the entire global job market, above all its challenges, and above the global order to wreck and smash the backup profession .. None of this found any use. All of it was gone with the wind. All of it was utterly destroyed .. So do not think with the mentality of the distressed who are afflicted, surrounded by the cutting off of provision, because you will perish with them; raise the degree of your nearness to your Great Lord, for if you truly do so you will see wonders, not a single wonder. And remember that many of the poor do not want to draw near to Allah the Exalted; that is why many of the poor imitate one another even in this!""")

h(29, 1000, """Suffering from poverty is caused by imitating the poor""")

t(29, 1760, """The prophets were a light that many of those around them did not see, and the righteous on earth are still hardly seen by anyone around them! How many a misguided one millions think righteous, how many a caller at the gates of Hell whom many people follow, how many a blind of insight whose deviant thought people rub themselves against for blessing .. It is Hell being made ready, so let everyone of understanding beware!""")

h(29, 2250, """All the burdens of this world fell away from the one who knew!""")

t(30, 500, """Most people misunderstand this world because of the temporal creation specific to the earth. Since the earth is a land of experiments, not a land where states stay fixed, it and its people turn about in illusory temporal states, so that 10 years and 20 years are times people see as long, and even more so in human life when they imagine the state will stay fixed for 30 and 50 years, and this is reflected in their understanding of the reality of the world. Yet 100 years is within a created time, not a real time. The times of the people of the earth were created by our Great Lord, holy are His names and attributes, great in the heavens and on earth, exalted greatly, so that man may organize his journey on earth as life and then death. But man's failure to understand the reality of time in this world makes him feel the states of the world are fixed, so he lives many mental and psychological illusions and runs in this world as wild beasts run in the wilderness. Whereas the one who understands and realizes, you will find him in it calm and at peace, as if he owned the whole world. The root of attaining wisdom is the clarity of the spring, and your spring will not be clear until you remove every stone from it, and people's illusions are stones that keep them from wisdom. When you attain wisdom, the turbidity of the world leaves you, you pass the people of the world, and they are left lagging behind you while imagining they are ahead of you 😀""")

h(30, 1400, """The world is a land of experiments, and it is impossible for the results of experiments to stay fixed forever!""")

t(30, 2140, """Your affair as a human being in the abode of this world is set right only in the light of Allah the Exalted""")

h(30, 2350, """Light is never worldly! Rather it is of the Hereafter, and by it the affair of this world and the Hereafter is set right!""")

t(31, 770, """Every individual experience represents the making of a particular mental and psychological perception, because every person receives the results of his own experience according to his rules of thinking, affected by the accumulation of his psychological and mental store; affected by the negative or positive role of others around him in their direct and indirect influence on his understanding of the experience itself, his grasp of its results, and his perception of what was right and wrong in it; illuminated by the light of a wise person who lives in his surroundings and guides him, or blinded by the darkness of a fool who lives in his surroundings, misleads him and blinds him. That is why the way out is always in following the command of our Great Lord, holy are His names and attributes, great in the heavens and on earth, exalted greatly, for our Great Lord has commanded us to keep the company of those whose way Allah the Exalted has lit. Every day we read in the Book of our Great Lord: "And follow the way of the one who turns to Me." And we read: "Guide us to the straight path, the path of those You have blessed." And we read the saying of our Great Lord: "And keep yourself patient with those who call upon their Lord morning and evening, seeking His Face, and let not your eyes pass beyond them" """)

h(31, 1600, """People differ because of the uniqueness of their perceptions, which are built on the particularities of their experiences!""")

t(31, 2290, """A weak report in Kitab al-Fitan, stopping at the Basran Tabi'i Jaylan.

In the report:
Marhum al-Attar narrated to us, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, from Abu al-Jald Jaylan, who said: "A trial will befall the people of Islam while the people around them graze in plenty, until the Muslim will turn back a Jew or a Christian out of hardship."

The sign has occurred, and we see it fulfilled every day by the apostasy of those who apostatize among those who went to Western countries, even though, praise be to Allah our Lord, they are a very small minority whose numerical value is zero.""")

t(32, 110, """I was asked about the effect of football on world events! There is no effect.""")

h(32, 550, """The sign has occurred in general! And football does not prevent it!""")

t(32, 1320, """One of the ignorant is promoting on the internet that the noble ethics of prophethood require ((that a person not become angry for himself at all, ever, and never express his human pain no matter how much he is harmed)), and that if he becomes angry and has a human reaction by expressing his pain, by blame or by reproach, he is not a righteous person and there is disease in his heart!

This ignorant man, promoting a thought contrary to human nature, does not distinguish between the anger of the Prophet ﷺ as a human being, and his expression of his sorrow and pain as a person, and his not taking revenge, because he is certainly a prophet of pure soul, who forgives, pardons and does not take revenge.

First: Imam Muslim narrated in his Sahih that the Prophet ﷺ said: "O Allah, Muhammad is only a human being; he becomes angry as humans become angry." This hadith clearly proves that he ﷺ had natural human feelings.

Second: Abu Sufyan ibn al-Harith was the cousin of the Prophet ﷺ and his foster brother (Halimah al-Sa'diyyah nursed them both); he was among the people who most resembled the Prophet ﷺ and was his close childhood friend.

When the Prophet ﷺ was sent, this intense love of Abu Sufyan turned into a terrible enmity; he satirized the Prophet ﷺ in harsh poems and fought Islam for 20 years on every field.

Shortly before the Prophet ﷺ entered Mecca as a conqueror, Abu Sufyan ibn al-Harith came out with his son, repentant and Muslim, to meet the Prophet ﷺ on the road. When the Prophet ﷺ saw him, he turned his face away from him and shunned him.
Abu Sufyan tried to come to him from the other side, and the Prophet ﷺ turned his face away once again.
And because our noble Prophet ﷺ is a human being, the shunning here represents "reproach and human pain" at being let down by a relative and a lifelong friend, for a wound that comes from relatives and cousins is more painful and has a stronger effect on the soul.

Abu Sufyan complained of this shunning to Imam Ali ibn Abi Talib, peace be upon him, and to the Prophet's wife Umm Salamah""")

t(33, 60, """(she was his paternal half-sister). Imam Ali ibn Abi Talib advised him to come to the Prophet from in front of his face and say to him what the brothers of Yusuf, peace be upon him, said to him: "They said: By Allah, Allah has certainly preferred you over us, and we were indeed sinners." When Abu Sufyan did that, the gentle, merciful human heart of the Prophet ﷺ softened, he swallowed his old pain, and he answered him at once with the ethics of the prophets: "No blame upon you today; Allah will forgive you, and He is the Most Merciful of the merciful."

The Prophet's ﷺ turning his face away from his cousin is human behavior, human feelings, and an expression of anger, and it is the gentlest kind of reproach from a leader of a nation who possesses far more means than merely turning his face away; but these are the ethics of the Prophet, the Seal of the Messengers ﷺ.

For 20 years the Prophet's ﷺ cousin insulted him and wronged him, then the Prophet ﷺ says to him: I have forgiven you! A forgiveness that came after showing displeasure with the deed, so that the wrongdoer would know his wrong, and this is part of the Prophet's ﷺ upbringing of the Ummah.""")

h(33, 1000, """Dervishes or liars?! Pretenders of distorted thought!""")

t(33, 1720, """I do not recognize the satanic, Dajjalic sciences of energy. As for this post, the word energy in it means people's souls being affected by one another in something resembling transmitted energy .. as when you are in a place where there is an angry person, and you are affected by the energy of his negative self .. Likewise a cheerful person in a place spreads a feeling that suits his behavior; call it energy if you like, or call it a transmitted feeling, no problem. Likewise in a morally dissolute society the rate of souls being drawn toward dissolution increases, and in a morally committed society the rate of souls being drawn toward commitment increases. So the effect of collective energy exists, and this effect is not on all the inhabitants of a society. You will find a morally dissolute person in a committed society, but he resists commitment and is tired and exhausted by the clean collective energy of the society; and you will find a morally committed person in a dissolute society, and he resists dissolution and is tired and exhausted by the unclean collective energy prevailing in a society. You will find the morally dissolute society attracting more of those who abandon morals and love to abandon them, and it will also attract those who love morals but have grown tired of keeping to them because their souls are weak. The matter is not mere imitation; rather, there is an attracting energy that pulls new souls and pushes them strongly toward moral disintegration. The greatest of these in effect is direct face-to-face energy, and second in effect is the deeply influential "energy of screens," which comes second after the energy of direct physical proximity, such as watching moral disintegration in a street, a restaurant, a closed building, open squares, or places of public or private gathering!""")

h(34, 300, """The energy of the environment is a reality! Collective energy has a great influence on the individual's behavior!""")

